Microsoft Word is a popular word processing software program developed by Microsoft that allows users to create,
edit, format, and share professional text documents.Key Features and UsesDocument Creation: Build resumes, reports, letters, 
and school assignments.Rich Formatting: Change fonts, colors, alignments, and insert tables or images.Collaboration: Use "Track Changes" 
and comments to work with others in real-time.File Extensions: Save files typically as .doc or .docx.Interface BasicsTitle Bar:
Shows the file name at the top.Ribbon Tabs: Organizes tools into functional areas like Home, Insert, and Layout.Workspace: 
The main blank area where you type your text.Status Bar: Displays page numbers, word count, and zoom
controls at the bottom.AvailabilityPlatforms: Available for Windows, macOS, iOS, Android, 
and web browsers.Access: Offered via a Microsoft 365 subscription or as a standalone purchase.
